<title>HONG KONG: Hanil Bank's FRN issue freed to trade.</title>
<headline>Hanil Bank's FRN issue freed to trade.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hanil Bank's US$200 million three-year floating rate note issue is now free to trade, lead manager Fuji International Finance (HK) said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The notes, which were launched this morning, were free to trade at 3.00 pm local time (0700 GMT).</p>
<p>The notes were issued and re-offered at 99.97 and float at 21 basis points over the six-month London Interbank Offered Rate.</p>
<p>Fees are 14 basis points.</p>
<p>In addition to Fuji, lead managers are Barclays de Zoete Wedd, Lehman Brothers, LTCB Asia and Sanwa International Finance.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843-6371</p>
